Translation patch: `proto::codec::trusted` (new module: the trust boundary of the compressed codec)

Change: Adds `src/proto/codec/trusted.rs`, declared `pub(crate) mod trusted` in `codec/mod.rs`, with one function per dependency operation the compressed codec uses: `compression_none` (`Compression::none()`), `compression_eq` (the derived `==` of `Compression`), `compress_new` (`Compress::new(level, true)`), `decompress_new` (`Decompress::new(true)`), `deflate` and `inflate` (the bodies of upstream `deflate_into` / `inflate_into`, writing into a fresh `Vec` of the same length instead of the spare capacity of the destination `BytesMut`, and returning it), and `vec_capacity` (`Vec::capacity`).
Why: The module is `opaque` in Cargo.toml (the pattern of patch 40), so the trusted surface of the compressed codec is exactly this list, each with a Lean model or axiom in `FunsExternal.lean`. flate2 is a dependency (not translated), `Compress`/`Decompress` hold foreign state, and upstream `deflate_into`/`inflate_into` write through raw pointers into uninitialised spare capacity (`unsafe`, `slice_from_raw_parts_mut`, `advance_mut`), which Aeneas cannot model. `Vec::capacity` has no Aeneas model.
Behaviour: Unchanged: the module is not used until the next patch. (`deflate`/`inflate` are compared with the functions they replace in patch 121.)

